[b]GoneSmart – Smart Auto-DJ, Audio Profiles & GMMP Extensions[/b]

Hi everyone,

I'd like to share [b]GoneSmart[/b], an independent Xposed/libxposed module and companion app that extends GoneMAD Music Player with a smarter Auto-DJ and optional audio, playlist and playback features.

I'll keep this first post updated and use the thread replies for future releases.

[b]GitHub:[/b]
[url=https://github.com/alagga/GoneSmart]https://github.com/alagga/GoneSmart[/url]

[b]Current release:[/b]
[url=https://github.com/alagga/GoneSmart/releases/tag/v0.5.0-rc.1]GoneSmart v0.5.0-rc.1[/url]


[b]What is GoneSmart?[/b]

GoneSmart keeps GMMP as the actual music player and adds extra functionality around it. Smart Auto-DJ combines relationships from your own normal GMMP playlists with ListenBrainz and Last.fm, then matches recommendations against music that already exists in your local GMMP library. Your complete music library is not uploaded to those services.


[b]Main features[/b]

[b]Smart Auto-DJ[/b]
• Session-aware recommendations based on the current and recently selected tracks
• Local Playlist Affinity + ListenBrainz + Last.fm
• Smart defaults plus optional Custom provider controls
• Controlled variety, rating/matching preferences and recommendation caching
• Only selects music that exists in your GMMP library
• Optional fallback to GMMP's normal Auto-DJ
• Player indicator showing GoneSmart Auto-DJ status

[b]Bluetooth Audio Profiles[/b]
• Different GMMP Equalizer and Effects overrides for remembered Bluetooth outputs
• Normal no-Bluetooth GMMP state remains Standard
• Automatic Standard/Bluetooth restoration when outputs change
• GMMP Equalizer presets, PRE and adaptive 2–10-band layouts
• Individual Effects overrides such as Balance, Limiter, Bass boost, Tempo, Virtualizer and Amplifier

[b]Playlist & Smart-Playlist tools[/b]
• Playlist folders and Smart-Playlist folders
• Multi-selection
• Playlist Link – use a normal playlist as a live source inside a Smart Playlist

[b]Playback tools[/b]
• Flip the current queue
• Play normal playlists or Smart Playlists from last track to first
• Track Auto-DJ – start a new Smart Auto-DJ session directly from an individual song

[b]Companion app[/b]
• Module and GMMP status
• Smart DJ, Audio Profiles and UI settings
• Compatibility information
• High-level activity/error logs
• Update checking and built-in help


[b]Current compatibility[/b]

• [b]GoneSmart:[/b] v0.5.0-rc.1
• [b]Tested GMMP version:[/b] 4.2.1
• [b]Android:[/b] 8.0+
• [b]Hooking API:[/b] libxposed API 102
• [b]Recommended rooted setup:[/b] JingMatrix Vector 2.2+

LSPatch v1.2 is documented as a possible no-root setup, but it has [b]not been tested by me[/b] and should be treated as experimental.


[b]Important[/b]

GoneSmart is an [b]independent project[/b] and is not affiliated with GoneMAD Software.

If you run into something that looks like a GMMP bug, please disable GoneSmart first and check whether the problem can still be reproduced with normal GMMP before reporting it to the GMMP developer. If it only happens with GoneSmart enabled, please report it here or on the GoneSmart GitHub instead.


[b]GMMP updates[/b]

GoneSmart integrates with GMMP internals, so a future GMMP update can temporarily break compatibility. I recommend disabling automatic Play Store updates for GMMP and checking the tested GMMP version here or on GitHub before updating manually. GoneSmart also warns when it detects a different GMMP version.


[b]0.5.0 release candidate[/b]

The 0.5.0 candidate combines Bluetooth Audio Profiles, the smarter Auto-DJ provider blend and the accepted GMMP 4.2.1 Playlist Link / Track Auto-DJ compatibility work. The release candidate is for combined testing before the stable 0.5.0 release.


[b]Feedback & bug reports[/b]

Feedback is very welcome, especially with different libraries, Bluetooth outputs, Android setups and GMMP configurations. If something breaks, please include your exact GMMP version and, if possible, the relevant GoneSmart logs.

[url=https://github.com/alagga/GoneSmart/issues]GitHub issues and feature requests[/url]

GoneSmart is an independent project and is not affiliated with GoneMAD Software, Last.fm, MusicBrainz, MetaBrainz or ListenBrainz.
